    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58674" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολόκῡμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>large heavy wave</i> before it breaks, <i>swell</i> that
			is the forerunner of a storm: metaph., of the swelling threats of
			Cleon, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				692
			</span></i> (expld. as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόλον κῦμα</span>,
			Sch.ad loc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλὸν κῦμα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωφὸν κῦμα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>).</div>
